sentences.l:
In Chen they were cut off from provisions;
those following him fell ill,
and none could get up.

Zilu came before him, resentful, and said: “Does the gentleman too have his straits?”
The Master said: “The gentleman indeed has his straits;
the small man in straits spills over.”

Standing, one sees them ranged before one;
in the carriage, one sees them leaning on the yoke-bar —
then, and only then, one gets through.

The Master said: “Straight indeed, Shi Yu!
When the state had the Way, like an arrow;
when the state lacked the Way, like an arrow.”

A gentleman indeed, Qu Boyu!
When the state had the Way, he took office;
when the state lacked the Way, he could roll it up and keep it in his breast.

The Master said: “The officer of purpose, the humane man:
none seeks life at the cost of harming humaneness;
some give up their lives to make humaneness complete.”

The Master said: “The gentleman is troubled by having no ability;
he is not troubled by others' not knowing him.”
The Master said: “The gentleman is pained at coming to the end of his days and his name not spoken of.”

Understanding reaches it,
humaneness can keep it;
if one does not oversee them with gravity,
then the people are not respectful.
